{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.BWVacuumRowFibre","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BWVacuumRowFibre","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Normed.Field.Basic"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.bwS0N_norm_off_unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.bwS0N_norm_off_unit","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowFibre.lean#L90-L99","doc":"**Contrast lemma — the open object, made explicit.**  Off the fibre root of unity, at `‖q‖ = r`,\nthe modulus of the concrete row is `‖s0‖·r^{c·f}`: the framing factor `r^{c·f}` survives and does\n**NOT** cancel unless `c·f = 0`.  At the observable archimedean `q₀ > 1` (`r = q₀ > 1`) this restates\nthe #3662 refutation — for the forced Seifert framing `f ≠ 0` and a non-self-conjugate block\n(`c ≠ 0`), `r^{c·f} ≠ 1`, so `‖bwS0N‖ ≠ ‖s0‖`.  The open residue is precisely the continuation\n`r = 1 → r = q₀`; this lemma locates that frontier and asserts no physics beyond it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.bwS0N_normSq_eq_verlinde","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.bwS0N_normSq_eq_verlinde","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowFibre.lean#L78-L86","doc":"**Capstone: the squared modulus of the geometric vacuum row realizes the Verlinde measure `W_λ` at\nthe fibre.**  `‖bwS0N‖² = ‖s0‖²` — independent of the framing `f`.  With `s0 = S_{0λ} = d_q/D` this is\n`W_λ = S_{0λ}² = d_q²/D²` (`KeystoneVerlindeSMatrixBridge.verlindeMeasure`).  So at the fibre root of\nunity `‖q‖ = 1` the geometric squared-amplitude **is** the Verlinde measure, framing-cancelled — the\nsurviving residue of the #3662 refutation.  This does not close the gate; it states precisely what\nsurvives at `‖q‖ = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.bwS0N_norm_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.bwS0N_norm_eq","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowFibre.lean#L69-L76","doc":"**The framing cancels in the modulus at the fibre root of unity.**  `‖bwS0N‖ = ‖s0·(θ)^f‖ =\n‖s0‖·‖θ‖^{f} = ‖s0‖·1^{f} = ‖s0‖`: at `‖q‖ = 1` the framing `θ^f` is a phase, so the modulus of the\nconcrete vacuum row is exactly the modulus of the S-matrix entry `s0` — the framing dependence drops\nout. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.thetaN_norm_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.thetaN_norm_one","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowFibre.lean#L62-L67","doc":"**The twist is a phase at the fibre root of unity.**  If `‖q‖ = 1` then `‖θ_λ‖ = ‖q^{c}‖ =\n‖q‖^{c} = 1`.  This is the fibre-level statement `Im q ≠ 0` (AGENTS.md fibre-vs-observable `q`): at\n`‖q‖ = 1` the twist carries no modulus, only a phase. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.bwS0N","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.bwS0N","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowFibre.lean#L55-L58","doc":"**The concrete RT / Seifert vacuum row over a normed field** `bwS0N = s0·(θ)^{f}`: the S-matrix\nvacuum entry `s0` times the ribbon twist `θ = q^{c}` raised to the Seifert framing `f : ℤ`.  The\nnormed-field analogue of `BWVacuumRowConcrete.bwS0Concrete`, at the fibre variable `q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.thetaN","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.thetaN","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowFibre.lean#L51-L53","doc":"**The ribbon twist over a normed field** `θ = q^{c}`, with the block content sum `c : ℤ` carried\nas the datum (avoids re-deriving `contentSum`).  A `zpow` (the content sum may be negative). ","signatureChunk":0}]}